# Cline — Lens Design System Rules

## Mandate
This project uses ONLY `@loomhq/lens@12.14.0`. No other UI library permitted.

## Before Writing Any UI Code
Read: .lens-knowledge-base/QUICK-REFERENCE.md

## Critical Differences From Common Libraries
| Need | Wrong | Correct |
|------|-------|---------|
| Container/Box | `<div>`, `<Box>` | `<Container>` |
| Flex layout | `<Flex>`, flex div | `<Split>` + `<SplitSection>` |
| Grid layout | `<Grid>`, grid div | `<Arrange columns={[...]}>` |
| All headings | `<h1>`,`<Heading>` | `<Text size="heading-lg" htmlTag="h1">` |
| Disabled state | `disabled` | `isDisabled` |
| Loading state | `loading` | `hasLoader` |
| Element type | `as="a"` | `htmlTag="a"` |
| Button icons | `leftIcon` | `iconBefore` |
| Ref forwarding | `ref={ref}` | `refHandler={(r) => ref.current = r}` |
| Icon usage | Any SVG directly | `<Icon icon={<SvgName />} />` |

## Absolute Prohibitions
- No raw `<button>`, `<input>`, `<a>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>`
- No `style={{}}` inline styles
- No `className` with custom classes
- No CSS files, SCSS files, styled-components, Tailwind
- No imports from other UI libraries

## Decision Algorithm
1. Identify UI element needed
2. Check .lens-knowledge-base/COMPONENT-INDEX.md — does Lens have it?
3. YES → use it per .lens-knowledge-base/components/<Name>.md
4. NO → build wrapper with Lens layout + var(--lns-*) tokens
5. Pattern repeats → mark // TODO: [LENS-GAP] and report

## Reference
- Component lookup: .lens-knowledge-base/QUICK-REFERENCE.md
- Full component list: .lens-knowledge-base/COMPONENT-INDEX.md
- Component details: .lens-knowledge-base/components/<Name>.md
- Tokens: .lens-knowledge-base/tokens/_tokens-index.md
- Full governance: AGENTS.md
